            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>A puka's true form is unknown to all, save perhaps the Eldest. These private and tricksy shapeshifters almost always wear another shape, and they're invisible when not transformed. Pukas most commonly appear as fine black horses with golden eyes, often in full tack, approaching unsuspecting mortals and enticing them to take a ride. When a puka succeeds in coaxing a rider onto their back, they launch into a gallop far faster than any horse could sprint, taking their unfortunate rider on a wild and terrifying—but ultimately harmless—journey before dropping them off exactly where they were picked up. They play similar pranks in their other forms: leading hunters on a merry chase through darkened woods as a fox or wolf, tempting late-night tavern goers as a beautiful humanoid, or taunting mortal animals as an uncatchable hare.</p>\n<p>Any animal form a puka takes is covered in slick black fur. Even in their humanoid guises, their hair remains similarly shiny and dark, and they always include some tell-tale animalistic features, such as a horse's ears or a fox's tail.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
        },
